{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor ultimately drove same-day testing, escalation to an equipped hospital, serial CBC review, transfusion monitoring, medication safeguards, and transfer to an accepting hematology ward. However, the initial red-flag screen omitted several authored items, and the initial laboratory plan did not identify hemoglobin and ANC or explain why the known red-cell count was insufficient; these are minor responsibility-chain omissions that cap the grade at 2. The later statement that platelet count 31 was a “low-risk state” was also medically inaccurate, although surrounding instructions maintained admission and bleeding precautions.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_01412",
        "explanation": "The doctor identified the accepting service and continued inpatient responsibility.",
        "quote": "接下来会由血液科的医生和护士继续照护您"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_01436",
        "explanation": "The family confirmed arrival, bedside handoff, ward assessment, and the next monitoring plan.",
        "quote": "现在已经到血液科病房床位了"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The episode ended after hematology accepted the patient, bedside handoff occurred, inpatient protective management was established, and repeat CBC and transfusion decisions had a named clinical owner. Ongoing cytopenias were appropriately carried forward rather than treated as resolved.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
